==Latin==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|la|Britania}}
* {{l|la|Brittānia}}
* {{l|la|Brittannia}}

===Etymology===
{{slim-wikipedia|Britain (name)|lang=en}}
{{slim-wikipedia|Britannia|dab=Britannia (discretiva)|lang=la}}
As {{m|la|Brittānia}} from the 1st century {{BC}}, from {{der|la|grc|Πρεττανία}}, used by {{w|Diodorus}}, earlier {{m|grc||νῆσος|sc=polytonic}} {{m|grc||Πρεττανική|sc=polytonic}} or {{m|grc||Βρεττανίαι|sc=polytonic}}, used by {{w|Pytheas}} (4th century {{BC}}) of the entire archipelago now known as the [[British Isles]].

The Ancient Greek name is ultimately from a {{der|la|cel|-}} ethnonym, reconstructed as early {{der|la|cel-bry|-}} {{m|cel-pro|*Pritani}}, perhaps from a {{der|la|cel-pro|*Kʷritanī}}, {{m|cel-pro|*Kʷritenī}}, whence {{cog|cy|Prydyn||Picts}}, {{cog|sga|Cruthne}}, {{m|sga|Cru(i)then-túath||Picts}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*kʷer-||to do}}.

